      "chunks": [
        {
          "chunk_index": 1,
          "chunk_id": "s01_c01",
          "anchor_id": "cue_s01_c1_recurrent_neural_networks_workhorse",
          "text": "Recurrent neural networks are a workhorse for sequence data, yet they famously struggle when the data carries long-term dependencies. This paper asks why, from the rigorous viewpoint of approximation theory.",
          "expected_role": "method",
          "cue_keywords": [
            "recurrent",
            "neural",
            "networks",
            "workhorse",
            "sequence",
            "yet",
            "they",
            "famously",
            "struggle",
            "when"
          ],
          "required": true
        },
        {
          "chunk_index": 2,
          "chunk_id": "s01_c02",
          "anchor_id": "cue_s01_c2_authors_prove_inverse_bernstein_type",
          "text": "The authors prove an inverse, or Bernstein-type, theorem for nonlinear RNNs: any sequence relationship that can be stably approximated by an RNN must have a memory that decays exponentially in time.",
          "expected_role": "method",
          "cue_keywords": [
            "authors",
            "prove",
            "inverse",
            "bernstein-type",
            "theorem",
            "nonlinear",
            "rnns",
            "any",
            "sequence",
            "relationship"
          ],
          "required": true
        },
        {
          "chunk_index": 3,
          "chunk_id": "s01_c03",
          "anchor_id": "cue_s01_c3_other_words_difficulty_not_just",
          "text": "In other words, the difficulty is not just an optimization artifact, it is a fundamental limitation of the RNN hypothesis space, extending the known curse of memory from linear to nonlinear networks.",
          "expected_role": "method",
          "cue_keywords": [
            "other",
            "words",
            "difficulty",
            "not",
            "just",
            "optimization",
            "artifact",
            "fundamental",
            "limitation",
            "rnn"
          ],
          "required": true
        },
        {
          "chunk_index": 4,
          "chunk_id": "s01_c04",
          "anchor_id": "cue_s01_c4_building_analysis_they_propose_princ",
          "text": "Building on this analysis, they propose a principled stable reparameterization that lets RNNs escape the limitation, and they confirm everything with numerical experiments.",
          "expected_role": "method",
          "cue_keywords": [
            "building",
            "analysis",
            "they",
            "propose",
            "principled",
            "stable",
            "reparameterization",
            "lets",
            "rnns",
